Can you stay cool enough in this market?
Crypto assets carry high risks, this is just a market update, not trading advice.

#Key Bullish/Bearish Observation Signals (Determine Future Market Direction)
Bullish Reversal Confirmation Signals (Must meet at least 2 conditions for a trend rebound foundation)
1. US CPI and PCE inflation data significantly drop, market re-prices for a rate cut in September;
2. BTC spot ETF ends consecutive outflows, showing three consecutive days of net inflow;
3. BTC holds above $68,000, ETH/BTC ratio rebounds and breaks above 0.029, altcoin season index rises above 75;
4. 10-year US Treasury yields continue to drop, dollar index weakens.

Bearish Continuation Risk Signals (Any one condition being met will open downside potential)
1. Inflation data rebounds, Fed releases further tightening language;
2. BTC effectively falls below the critical support of $60,000, triggering a chain of leveraged liquidations;
3. Mt. Gox large chips concentrated sell-off, ETF outflow continues to expand;
4. US crypto regulatory bill introduces stricter clauses, suppressing institutional entry expectations.

Layered Trading Strategies (Distinguishing Spot/Contracts/Allocation)
1. Mid to long-term positioning in spot (no high leverage)
 Position Control: Total capital allocation not exceeding 40%, keeping stablecoins as cash to wait for extreme fear zones to increase positions;
​Asset Selection: Only allocate core leaders BTC and ETH, light positions in RWA compliant track leaders, avoiding unproven, large unlock small coins;
​Gradual Allocation Range: BTC $60,000–$62,000 as the first gradient accumulation zone, increase positions below $58,000, strictly tiered, no full position at once.

Short-term Contract Traders (High Risk Warning)
 The current market is highly volatile, with rapid switching between bulls and bears, high leverage can easily result in liquidation:
1. Lower leverage to within 5–10x, avoid full positions above 20x;
2. Don't chase pumps on small coins, focus on high selling and low buying around BTC and ETH;
3. In extreme fear index zones, do not blindly bottom buy, wait for stabilization signals before entering, set strict stop-loss;
4. Actively reduce positions before geopolitical events and US market data releases to avoid sudden and severe volatility.

Risk Avoidance Red Lines
1. Stay away from small coins with short-term gains exceeding 30% and continuous outflows on-chain;
2. Avoid projects with significant team or investor token unlocks within the last 30 days;
3. Do not heavily invest in MEME coins, lacking long-term value support, with the market entirely dependent on short-term sentiment. #BTC #ETH
